# Citta
## Bhūmi (Realms / Domains / Strata / Sphere)
- **Kāmabhūmi** (11 realms): the 4 apāya (woeful states), the human realm (manussaloka), and the 6 sensuous deva realms (devaloka)
- **Rūpabhūmi** (16 realms): from Brahma pārisajja to Akaniṭṭha. In the asaññasatta brahma realm citta does not arise
- **Arūpabhūmi** (4 arūpa realms)
- **Lokuttarabhūmi** (maggacitta, phalacitta, their associated cetasikas, and Nibbāna)

<hr style="width: 40%; margin: 1rem auto; border: 1px solid #AD6100;">

### Meaning of Loka here
Refers to the Lokiya Saṅkhata Dhammas (mundane conditioned phenomena)

**Lokiya / Lokuttara x Saṅkhata / Asaṅkhata:**
- **Lokiya saṅkhata dhammas**: nāmas and rūpas except magga- and phala-cittacetasikas and Nibbāna
- **Lokiya asaṅkhata dhammas**: do not exist
- **Lokuttara saṅkhata dhammas**: magga and phala cittacetasikas
- **Lokuttara asaṅkhata dhamma**: Nibbāna

---

## Cittas According to Bhūmi
- **Kāmāvacaracitta** (consciousness of the sense sphere)
- **Rūpāvacaracitta** (consciousness of the fine-material sphere)
- **Arūpāvacaracitta** (consciousness of the immaterial sphere)
- **Lokuttaracitta** (supramundane consciousness): consciousness that transcends (magga) or has transcended (phala) the conditioned world

<hr style="width: 40%; margin: 1rem auto; border: 1px solid #AD6100;">

